  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I need to find a rule connecting input to output:\n\n1. **Anomaly detection**: Find the non-0, non-5, non-7 color (it replaces a 5)\n2. **Grid structure**: The 5s form a grid of rectangular cells\n3. **Walls**: 7s between adjacent 5-grid-points create walls between cells\n4. **Connected components**: Cells without walls between them form connected groups\n5. **Fully enclosed component**: Find the component where ALL boundary edges have walls\n6. **Draw**: Replace that component's area with the anomaly color border (8-connected) and clear interior; fix the anomaly back to 5\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    anomaly_color, anomaly_pos, five_positions = None, None, set()\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 5: five_positions.add((r, c))\n            elif v not in (0, 7):\n                anomaly_color, anomaly_pos = v, (r, c)\n                five_positions.add((r, c))\n    grid_rows = sorted(set(r for r, c in five_positions))\n    grid_cols = sorted(set(c for r, c in five_positions))\n    nr, nc = len(grid_rows) - 1, len(grid_cols) - 1\n    def has_wall(r1, c1, r2, c2):\n        if r1 == r2:\n            return any(grid[r1][c] == 7 for c in range(min(c1,c2)+1, max(c1,c2)))\n        return any(grid[r][c1] == 7 for r in range(min(r1,r2)+1, max(r1,r2)))\n    def idx(i, j): return i * nc + j\n    n = nr * nc\n    adj = [set() for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(nr):\n        for j in range(nc):\n            if j + 1 < nc:\n                ec = grid_cols[j+1]\n                if not has_wall(grid_rows[i], ec, grid_rows[i+1], ec):\n                    adj[idx(i,j)].add(idx(i,j+1)); adj[idx(i,j+1)].add(idx(i,j))\n            if i + 1 < nr:\n                er = grid_rows[i+1]\n                if not has_wall(er, grid_cols[j], er, grid_cols[j+1]):\n                    adj[idx(i,j)].add(idx(i+1,j)); adj[idx(i+1,j)].add(idx(i,j))\n    visited = [False] * n\n    components = []\n    for s in range(n):\n        if visited[s]: continue\n        comp, stack = [], [s]\n        while stack:\n            node = stack.pop()\n            if visited[node]: continue\n            visited[node] = True; comp.append(node)\n            for nb in adj[node]:\n                if not visited[nb]: stack.append(nb)\n        components.append(comp)\n    def is_enclosed(comp):\n        cs = set(comp)\n        for node in comp:\n            i, j = divmod(node, nc)\n            r1, c1, r2, c2 = grid_rows[i], grid_cols[j], grid_rows[i+1], grid_cols[j+1]\n            if (i == 0 or idx(i-1,j) not in cs) and not has_wall(r1, c1, r1, c2): return False\n            if (i == nr-1 or idx(i+1,j) not in cs) and not has_wall(r2, c1, r2, c2): return False\n            if (j == 0 or idx(i,j-1) not in cs) and not has_wall(r1, c1, r2, c1): return False\n            if (j == nc-1 or idx(i,j+1) not in cs) and not has_wall(r1, c2, r2, c2): return False\n        return True\n    target = None\n    for comp in components:\n        if is_enclosed(comp): target = comp; break\n    area = set()\n    if target:\n        for node in target:\n            i, j = divmod(node, nc)\n            for r in range(grid_rows[i], grid_rows[i+1]+1):\n                for c in range(grid_cols[j], grid_cols[j+1]+1):\n                    area.add((r, c))\n    output = copy.deepcopy(grid)\n    if anomaly_pos: output[anomaly_pos[0]][anomaly_pos[1]] = 5\n    for (r, c) in area:\n        border = any((r+dr, c+dc) not in area for dr in [-1,0,1] for dc in [-1,0,1] if dr or dc)\n        output[r][c] = anomaly_color if border else 0\n    return output\n```",
